    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d355">

                <pb facs="0424" n="406" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg406"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.24112 RP/1–2546: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Bolivia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Adam</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-03-09T14:00:00-05:00">March 9, 1946—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>131. Dept deplores attitude evidenced in the last paragraph urdes 2141 Jan 25
                    1946. True facts are IDPLC gave repeated and careful consideration Gundlach case
                    because it realized so thoroughly implications for Emb and replacement program.
                    IDPLC gave detailed account of inadequacies of reorganization so that Emb would
                    appreciate IDPLC position, moreover, IDPLC suggested possible solution of
                    impasse by suggesting Gundlach case could be reconsidered as part of overall
                        plan.<anchor n="99" xml:id="d355-f1"/></p>
                <p>Fortunately Dept prevented distribution of your despatch to other agencies of
                    Govt. Dept would have been most embarrassed if last paragraph had reached hands
                    of IDPLC.</p>
                <p>If Gundlach case is presented as part of an overall program pertinent info in
                    despatch, omitting last paragraph will be brought to attention of IDPLC.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d355-f1" n="99" xml:id="d355-f1-content">
                <p>In despatch 2385, March 14, 1946, the Chargé indicated his impression that the
                    position of the IDPLC did not coincide with the views of the Department of State
                    (740.24112 RP/3–1446).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
